diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index b7f9925..6754b2a 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 A growing SoC fabric for the Inspur YPCB-00338 (Kintex-7 `xc7k480t`) and other 7-series boards. Wishbone B4 pipelined throughout. Every IP gates on **formal verification + simulation + hardware witness** before it crosses the line.
 
-> **Status:** DDR3 channel 0 is validated on real YPCB-00338 hardware at a DDR3-800 operating point with deterministic, random, boundary, address-walking, data-bit/byte-lane, XOR checksum, and 600-second soak evidence. See `boards/ypcb-00338/DDR3_VALIDATION.md`.
+> **Current status:** The default image is the BRAM-only JTAG/Wishbone proof. The earlier DDR3 controller was removed; its channel-0 hardware results are preserved in `boards/ypcb-00338/DDR3_VALIDATION.md`. The replacement DDR3 implementation is still in init/MPR bring-up, with external DDR Wishbone storage blocked. See the [board guide](boards/ypcb-00338/README.md) and [Fedora preparation](docs/fedora-bringup.md).
 
 ## Repository layout
 
